## 7. Stimulus / Response Classification / 刺激与响应分类

- 实时系统必须对不规则间隔发生的事件（刺激）做出响应。
- Real-time systems have to respond to events occurring at irregular intervals.
- 这些事件（或刺激）通常会导致系统转移到不同的状态，因此可用于状态机建模。
- These events (or stimuli) often cause the system to move to a different state, thus may be used as a way of describing a state machine modeling real-time system.
- 看待实时系统的一种方式是将其视为一个刺激/响应（Stimulus/Response）系统。
- One way of looking at a real-time system is as a stimulus/response system.

### Two Classes of Stimulus / 两类刺激：
1. **周期性刺激 (Periodic Stimulus)**：
   - 发生在可预测的时间间隔内。
   - These occur at predictable time intervals.
   - 例如：系统每隔 50ms 检查一次传感器，并根据传感器数值（刺激）采取行动（响应）。
   - E.g., the system will examine a sensor every 50ms & take action (respond) depending on the sensor value (stimulus).

2. **非周期性刺激 (Aperiodic Stimulus)**：
   - 不规则地发生（通常使用计算机的中断机制发出信号）。
   - These occur irregularly (usually signaled using the computer's interrupt mechanism).
   - 例如：计算机系统中的 I/O 中断，表明 I/O 传输已完成且缓冲区中有可用数据。
   - E.g., I/O interrupt in a computer system indicating that an I/O transfer was complete & that data was available in a buffer.

